            <ul>
              <li><strong>X / Twitter</strong>: Go to Settings &gt; Your Account &gt; Download an archive of your data.
                The export contains a file named `bookmarks.js` or `bookmarks.json` in your data folder.</li>
              <li><strong>Instagram</strong>: Go to Account Center &gt; Your Information and Permissions &gt; Download
                your information. Request standard JSON format, select "Saved Items" only. Look for `saved_posts.json`
                inside the ZIP.</li>
              <li><strong>Threads</strong>: Use the SocialFeed extension on the Threads Saved page, then import its downloaded JSON package here.</li>
